{"name":"Red Ink","hex":"#ac3235","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red ink","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Financial loss.","Cheap red wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_ink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rubrication","blocks":[{"text":"Rubrication is the addition of text in red ink to a manuscript for emphasis. Practitioners of rubrication, so-called rubricators or rubrishers, were specialized scribes who received text from the original scribe. Rubrication was one of several steps in the medieval process of manuscript making. The term comes from the Latin rubrīcāre, \"to color red\", the base word being ruber, \"red\". The practice began in pharaonic Egypt with scribes emphasizing important text, such as headings, new parts of a narrative, etc., on papyri with red ink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Illuminated.bible.closeup.arp.jpg/330px-Illuminated.bible.closeup.arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubrication"},{"title":"Red Ink (1960 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Ink is a 1960 Hungarian romantic drama film directed by Viktor Gertler and starring Éva Vass, György Pálos and Nóra Tábori. It was shot at the Hunnia Studios in Budapest. The film's sets were designed by the art director József Romvári."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Red_Ink_%281960_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Ink_(1960_film)"},{"title":"Red Ink (2000 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Ink is a 2000 drama film directed by Francisco Lombardi from a screenplay written by Giovanna Pollarolo, based on the novel by Alberto Fuguet."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Ink_(2000_film)"},{"title":"Ink","blocks":[{"text":"Ink is a gel, sol, or solution that contains at least one colorant, such as a dye or pigment, and is used to color a surface to produce an image, text, or design. Ink is used for drawing or writing with a pen, brush, reed pen, or quill. Thicker inks, in paste form, are used extensively in letterpress and lithographic printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg/330px-F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/IncunabulumDetail.JPG/330px-IncunabulumDetail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/IncunabulumDetail.JPG/330px-IncunabulumDetail.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail from a rare Blackletter Bible (1497) printed and rubricated in Strasbourg by Johann Grüninger","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIncunabulumDetail.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Liturgical_codex_Louvre_E10094.jpg/500px-Liturgical_codex_Louvre_E10094.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Liturgical_codex_Louvre_E10094.jpg/1280px-Liturgical_codex_Louvre_E10094.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Liturgical_codex_Louvre_E10094.jpg/500px-Liturgical_codex_Louvre_E10094.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Extract of the second letter of St Paul to the Corinthians (2 Corinthians 6:5–7), and of the second letter of St Peter (2 Peter 2:4–5.7–9), with red ink for certain characters.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALiturgical_codex_Louvre_E10094.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo